  "instruction": "## Goal\nRestore the original behavior of `minidump.common_structs.MinidumpMemorySegment.aread` so it performs an asynchronous read from a file handler instead of raising `NotImplementedError`.\n\n## Observable behavior\n```python\n# Example 1: successful async read at the segment start\nseg = MinidumpMemorySegment()\nseg.start_virtual_address = 0x1000\nseg.size = 0x100\nseg.start_file_address = 0x0\nseg.end_virtual_address = 0x1100\n\ndata = b\"ABCDEFGH\" * 32\nfh = AsyncFakeFileHandler(data)\n\nresult = run_async(seg.aread(0x1000, 8, fh))\nassert result == b\"ABCDEFGH\"\n```\n\n```python\n# Example 2: async read with an offset inside the segment\nseg = MinidumpMemorySegment()\nseg.start_virtual_address = 0x1000\nseg.size = 0x100\nseg.start_file_address = 0x0\nseg.end_virtual_address = 0x1100\n\ndata = b\"01234567\" * 32\nfh = AsyncFakeFileHandler(data)\n\nresult = run_async(seg.aread(0x1004, 4, fh))\nassert result == b\"4567\"\n```\n\n## Constraints\n- The method to restore is `aread` on `minidump.common_structs.MinidumpMemorySegment`.\n- The signature must remain `aread(self, virtual_address, size, file_handler)`.\n- The implementation must be asynchronous (compatible with async file handlers that provide `tell`, `seek`, and `read` as coroutines).\n- Files in scope include `minidump/common_structs.py` and the rest of the `minidump/` package and tests.\n\n## How success is measured\nSuccess is measured by passing the verifier tests:\n```\npython -m pytest -q tests/generated/test_minidump_common_structs.py::TestMinidumpMemorySegmentAread::test_aread_cross_boundary_raises tests/generated/test_minidump_common_structs.py::TestMinidumpMemorySegmentAread::test_aread_offset tests/generated/test_minidump_common_structs.py::TestMinidumpMemorySegmentAread::test_aread_restores_position tests/generated/test_minidump_common_structs.py::TestMinidumpMemorySegmentAread::test_aread_success tests/generated/test_minidump_common_structs.py::TestMinidumpMemorySegmentAread::test_aread_wrong_segment_raises\n```",
